WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.409 --> 00:00:04.720
We’re entering the third year of the pandemic
and in the US

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:10.099
the loss of life, month by month, 
for two years, looks like this.

00:00:10.099 --> 00:00:13.743
Altogether more than 900,000 people have died.

00:00:15.632 --> 00:00:17.500
But there really are two pandemics here.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.070
Because starting in the spring of 2021

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:24.518
the distribution of the vaccines dramatically
changed the nature of the pandemic.

00:00:24.518 --> 00:00:27.429
If we look closer at the delta wave 
and the beginning of omicron

00:00:27.429 --> 00:00:32.592
we see the deaths of unvaccinated people were
much higher than vaccinated people.

00:00:32.592 --> 00:00:37.140
This data comes from a subset of US states
and cities that provide immunization data.

00:00:38.062 --> 00:00:40.553
While the delta wave did kill 
some vaccinated people

00:00:40.553 --> 00:00:44.357
the risk was 15 times higher 
if you were unvaccinated.

00:00:45.696 --> 00:00:48.707
Philly Baird was one of those 
unvaccinated people.

00:00:48.707 --> 00:00:52.204
And he started going live on his 
Facebook page from the hospital.

00:00:52.204 --> 00:00:54.379
"I love you guys."

00:00:54.379 --> 00:00:56.295
"I’m able to talk today."

00:00:57.767 --> 00:01:00.132
"Today’s been a great day."

00:01:00.944 --> 00:01:05.720
In one of the videos he recommends to his
friends and family that they get the vaccine.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.865
Do you think that was a 
hard thing for him to say?

00:01:08.865 --> 00:01:14.080
Yes, because that’s not what he had been
communicating, you know, prior to that.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.540
But I think that he would want me to communicate
what I know he wanted

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:20.930
and that is for you to look at his situation

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:23.729
and realize that you could possibly get

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:28.548
you could get severe the Covid like he did 
and be fighting for your life.

00:01:28.548 --> 00:01:32.900
And then have a lot of regrets that you didn’t
have the vaccine at that time.

00:01:35.249 --> 00:01:41.030
"You know I was one of those 
that sat there and kinda

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:44.428
was more on the political side with
Covid and all."

00:01:45.941 --> 00:01:48.277
"We gotta put all that aside."

00:01:55.390 --> 00:02:00.366
Now when it comes to the political breakdown
on vaccinations, there are two things to know.

00:02:00.366 --> 00:02:03.479
One is that a majority of Republicans are
vaccinated with at least 1 dose

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:07.250
according to the most recent survey 
from the Kaiser Family Foundation.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:12.476
The 2nd thing to know is that most 
unvaccinated Americans are Republican.

00:02:12.476 --> 00:02:16.200
So the question is: how does that affect the
balance of lives lost?

00:02:16.925 --> 00:02:20.470
Well, we can plot the states directly by their
2020 election results

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:24.179
with the red states on the right and the blue
states on the left.

00:02:24.179 --> 00:02:27.433
And we can look at their death rates since
April 2021.

00:02:27.433 --> 00:02:29.292
And it's pretty striking.

00:02:29.292 --> 00:02:33.182
The Republican states were suffering 
much bigger losses.

00:02:33.182 --> 00:02:37.258
And I want to stress that this relationship
wasn’t there before the vaccines.

00:02:37.258 --> 00:02:41.689
This is the same chart, but it shows death
rates before April 2021.

00:02:41.689 --> 00:02:46.854
And they’re much more spread out, with Covid
hitting blue states as hard as red ones.

00:02:46.854 --> 00:02:52.959
So what I want to understand is the series
of events that took us from this... to this.

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:58.210
"The Democrats are in a full-court freak out
over coronavirus

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:01.517
after Ted cruz self-isolated 
after coming into contact..."

00:03:01.517 --> 00:03:04.879
Phil Valentine was my younger brother.

00:03:04.879 --> 00:03:08.765
A very accomplished radio entertainment personality.

00:03:08.765 --> 00:03:11.880
"New York Times even called it the Trump virus."

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:15.910
"Can you imagine if the Ebola virus had been
called the Obama virus?"

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:20.060
He was on air in July and you can hear him
kind of talking through the symptoms.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.250
"This is my Covid saga."

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:26.193
"And yesterday was probably my worst day and
just the shaking and the chills..."

00:03:26.193 --> 00:03:28.359
Really processing things on air.

00:03:28.359 --> 00:03:31.712
"And as I’ve told you, I’m not judging
anybody either way."

00:03:31.712 --> 00:03:34.773
"If you want to get the vaccine, 
it’s a personal health decision."

00:03:34.773 --> 00:03:39.296
"I made the decision that I probably wouldn’t
die from it."

00:03:39.296 --> 00:03:44.620
"Phil would like his listeners to know that
he regrets not being more vehemently pro-vaccine."

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:47.760
"He is in the hospital in the critical-care
unit..."

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.411
He said, you know, I got it wrong.

00:03:51.411 --> 00:03:55.133
And then it went from bad to worse.

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:57.000
We know how it all ended.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:01.070
"We’re all very sad right now at the passing
of a friend and a colleague."

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:06.805
"And our thoughts and prayers go out to Susan
and the boys at their tremendous loss."

00:04:08.101 --> 00:04:11.390
Had he been opposed to other types of vaccines
in the past?

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.600
Were his or his kids vaccinated 
with the school vaccines?

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.272
He wasn't against anything else?

00:04:16.272 --> 00:04:17.272
No.

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:22.767
It’s not obvious that Republicans would
be more vaccine hesitant.

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:25.060
Similar percentages of Democrats and Republicans

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:29.120
said they get the flu shot “every year”
according to a May 2020 poll.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.450
And in 2019, the Pew Research Center 
found that

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:34.040
nearly identical shares of 
Republicans and Democrats

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.357
said that the benefits of the vaccinating
kids for measles, mumps, and rubella

00:04:37.357 --> 00:04:39.559
 outweigh the risks.

00:04:39.559 --> 00:04:43.059
Republicans were slightly less likely to say
they should be required

00:04:43.059 --> 00:04:45.172
but it’s nothing like the 
30 point gap

00:04:45.172 --> 00:04:49.722
that we see in Covid vaccination rates today.

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:53.850
One way to understand that gap is to consider
the vastly different information environments

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.230
that Republicans and Democrats live in.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:59.788
This is a list of news sources trusted by
at least 40% of Democrats

00:04:59.788 --> 00:05:01.867
according to a 2019 survey by Pew.

00:05:01.867 --> 00:05:04.023
"... health officials warn..."
"... the highest daily rate..."

00:05:04.023 --> 00:05:05.064
"... the Covid variant was first reported..."

00:05:05.064 --> 00:05:06.916
"... the latest data from the centers..."

00:05:06.916 --> 00:05:13.232
And here’s a list of news sources trusted
by at least 40% of Republicans.

00:05:13.232 --> 00:05:18.010
What this means is that American conservatives
are quite exposed to the editorial choices

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:19.458
of a single network.

00:05:19.458 --> 00:05:24.233
And on vaccine coverage, that network's choices
have been confusing.

00:05:24.233 --> 00:05:26.762
"It’s a great vaccine. It’s a safe vaccine."

00:05:26.762 --> 00:05:28.900
"It is something that can keep you out of
the hospital."

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:31.680
"How many people have been killed or injured
by the Covid vaccines?

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.059
Does anyone know the answer?"

00:05:33.059 --> 00:05:34.860
"If your doctor says you’re ok for it, 
get it.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:35.838
It will save your life."

00:05:35.838 --> 00:05:37.080
"I got my second dose.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.220
I got a horrific pain in my right eye."

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:41.700
"The vaccine is still working.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.160
It’s still protecting you and those around
you."

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:48.930
"Why should you penalize people for not taking
a vaccine which doesn’t work?"

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:52.020
"The mRNA covid vaccines need to be withdrawn
from the market now.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:53.432
No one should get them.

00:05:53.432 --> 00:05:54.812
No one should get boosted.

00:05:54.812 --> 00:05:55.678
No one should get double boosted."

00:05:55.678 --> 00:06:00.210
If we compare the information sources of those
who said they’d definitely get vaccinated

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:04.389
with the information sources of those who
said they would definitely not get vaccinated

00:06:04.389 --> 00:06:09.315
we see that the vaccine-resisters were less
likely to consume most news sources

00:06:09.315 --> 00:06:12.440
except for two:

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:15.483
Fox News and social media.

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:23.670
For 18 hours, I laid in bed 
dealing with my mortality

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.250
and not knowing which way 
that was going to go.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:28.800
And I'm laying in bed going, this is my fault.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:33.417
I should have been listening to doctors and
nurses and medical professionals

00:06:33.417 --> 00:06:36.967
 instead of my political algorithms.

00:06:36.967 --> 00:06:41.030
And so is it mostly Facebook where you were
getting sort of these messages?

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:42.030
Yes.

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:46.411
I saw some of Fox News reports online.

00:06:46.411 --> 00:06:52.490
But, 90 - 95 percent of what I got was through my
algorithms and friends on Facebook.

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:55.440
And I can tell you when I started 
telling people,

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:59.300
you need to consider this vaccine and 
you need to stop politicizing this.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:02.452
I lost a lot of friends, and the more hardcore
you were...

00:07:02.452 --> 00:07:04.800
I had some really ugly things said to me.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:09.206
And I had to start blocking people that I've
been friends with for years.

00:07:11.028 --> 00:07:15.150
The Kaiser Family Foundation found that 64%
of unvaccinated people

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:21.025
believed at least 4 pieces of Covid-19 misinformation,
of the 8 that they tested.

00:07:21.025 --> 00:07:23.919
And they found that among those who trusted
conservative news outlets

00:07:23.919 --> 00:07:30.178
belief in misinformation was more common than
among those who trusted other sources.

00:07:30.178 --> 00:07:32.669
But we have to remember that this is a correlation.

00:07:32.669 --> 00:07:36.127
We don’t know if anti-vax content 
on TV and Facebook 

00:07:36.127 --> 00:07:38.639
caused people to turn against the vaccine

00:07:38.639 --> 00:07:42.557
or if it was simply pandering to people who
had already made up their mind.

00:07:42.557 --> 00:07:44.028
It was probably both.

00:07:44.028 --> 00:07:46.005
See, one thing I didn’t mention 
about this chart 

00:07:46.005 --> 00:07:49.756
is that this data is actually 
from January 2021.

00:07:49.756 --> 00:07:54.177
So most of the anti-vaccine content on these
platforms hadn’t been published.

00:07:54.177 --> 00:07:57.449
So I went back and searched for 
the earliest polling I could find.

00:07:57.449 --> 00:07:59.019
This is from May of 2020

00:07:59.019 --> 00:08:03.027
and it asked people if they would get 
a hypothetical coronavirus vaccine.

00:08:03.027 --> 00:08:07.317
40 percent of Republicans said 
“definitely not or probably not.”

00:08:07.317 --> 00:08:12.000
And that’s pretty much where Republicans
are at today, 20 months later.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:18.080
So what explains why a big chunk of Republican
voters had already turned against the vaccine

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.971
six months before the presidential election

00:08:20.971 --> 00:08:25.449
and nearly a year before the vaccines 
were even available?

00:08:25.449 --> 00:08:27.896
I think the answer is somewhere in here.

00:08:27.896 --> 00:08:30.919
Of the 8 false claims polled by the Kaiser
Family Foundation

00:08:30.919 --> 00:08:35.148
the one most widely believed wasn’t about
the vaccines at all.

00:08:35.148 --> 00:08:41.120
And so of the different pieces of misinformation
we tested, the most commonly believed overall

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.940
and particularly by Republicans

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:48.370
was this idea that the government was inflating
the number of deaths due to Covid-19.

00:08:50.258 --> 00:08:54.770
"Top US health officials are rejecting President
Trump’s suggestion that the US coronavirus

00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:57.702
case and death totals are 'fake news'."

00:08:57.702 --> 00:09:00.738
"He said a couple of hours ago the number
of cases and deaths of the China virus..."

00:09:00.738 --> 00:09:03.150
"... are quote 'far exaggerated'."

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:06.000
That claim was based on a misunderstanding
of how death certificates work

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.700
but it was extremely potent.

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:11.847
If you’ve been told not to trust the death
count, how do you assess your own risk?

00:09:11.847 --> 00:09:15.770
And why would you take action to protect yourself
and your family?

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:19.600
If we compare unvaccinated republicans with
their vaccinated counterparts

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:22.880
the biggest difference between them isn’t
that the unvaccinated ones are younger or

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:24.870
more conservative or more rural

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:26.617
although they are

00:09:26.617 --> 00:09:28.443
it’s the pervasiveness of the belief 

00:09:28.443 --> 00:09:32.228
that seriousness of the coronavirus 
is generally exaggerated.

00:09:35.214 --> 00:09:39.120
And that idea that the pandemic has been made
into a bigger deal than it really is

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:43.089
has been an overarching belief for a majority
of Republicans.

00:09:43.089 --> 00:09:46.630
Even as Covid became one of the leading causes
of death in the US

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:51.644
even as the virus shifted 
from cities to rural America.

00:09:51.644 --> 00:09:54.760
And that takes us back to the very first weeks
of the pandemic.

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:59.905
When the virus found a United States under
an exceptionally polarizing president

00:09:59.905 --> 00:10:02.325
and at the start of an election year.

00:10:02.325 --> 00:10:05.340
"We have it under control. 
It’s going to be just fine."

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:08.880
"Joe Biden calling him the worst possible
person to lead our country through virus."

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:12.000
"Well we pretty much shut it down 
coming in from China."

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:15.810
"President Trump has no plan, no urgency,
no understanding of the facts."

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:19.160
"If the coronavirus ends up having a real
impact on the economy

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:20.423
 it could tip the election to the—"

00:10:20.423 --> 00:10:24.570
"Democrats and their media cronies have decided
to weaponize fear

00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:28.940
to improve their chances against Trump in
November."

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:32.900
In the early stages of the pandemic, you got
this very large polarization around things

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:36.357
like lockdowns, mask wearing, and the severity
of the pandemic itself.

00:10:36.357 --> 00:10:37.760
Just how seriously to take this.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:40.757
"Trump supported anti-lockdown protests..."

00:10:40.757 --> 00:10:43.200
"Liberate Minnesota, Michigan, and Virginia."

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.060
"...states led be Democratic governors."

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:46.427
"President Trump without a mask..."

00:10:46.427 --> 00:10:48.524
"Defiance in the face of adversity..."

00:10:48.524 --> 00:10:49.831
"Joe Biden wearing one."

00:10:49.831 --> 00:10:51.748
"...an image of trepidation, even fear."

00:10:51.748 --> 00:10:54.000
"Making for a splitscreen campaign moment."

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:57.260
And it seems that rank and file Republicans,
largely on their own, figured out that if

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.770
you don’t take the pandemic seriously, 
why would you get vaccinated?

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:02.262
You know the people telling you to do it,
they’re not trustworthy.

00:11:02.262 --> 00:11:06.412
And so, you know, flash forward to spring
of 2021 and you get this weird paradox where

00:11:06.412 --> 00:11:08.540
most Republican politicians are vaccinated

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:11.253
but they're saying stuff at the same time
to cater to

00:11:11.253 --> 00:11:12.933
to anti-vaccine sentiment in their base

00:11:12.933 --> 00:11:17.860
and now there's real political downside to
promoting vaccination for a lot of these folks.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.080
"...your freedoms, I do.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:20.238
You have to do what you have to do."

00:11:20.238 --> 00:11:23.412
"But! I recommend take the vaccines."

00:11:23.412 --> 00:11:24.522
"I did it. It's good."

00:11:24.522 --> 00:11:25.610
"Take the vaccines."

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:29.113
"But you got — no that's okay, that's alright."

00:11:29.113 --> 00:11:30.630
"You've got your freedoms..."

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:32.981
Let me tell you how I make sense 
of what happened to your brother 

00:11:32.981 --> 00:11:35.218
and I want to get your reaction.

00:11:35.218 --> 00:11:37.600
I see Phil looking at the data

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:40.750
concluding that his risk of dying 
from Covid was low.

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:45.140
But I think his brain was sort of pushed in
the direction of that conclusion by signals

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:51.190
that were sent really early on in the pandemic
by Trump and Fox and others that

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:54.480
Republicans kind of think this coronavirus
is overblown.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:56.906
The polarization starts there.

00:11:56.906 --> 00:11:59.480
Then by the time the vaccines come out

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:03.959
Phil's not getting clear, consistent signals
from the people that he trusts

00:12:03.959 --> 00:12:08.130
that it's time to update his risk calculation
and go ahead and get that vaccine.

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:12.230
And then he gets hit by the beginning 
of the delta wave.

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:13.735
Does that seem accurate to you?

00:12:13.735 --> 00:12:19.286
That's on the right track, I think that that...

00:12:19.286 --> 00:12:25.480
The calculus changed when the delta variant
presented itself because it attacked a much

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:28.244
younger segment of the population.

00:12:28.244 --> 00:12:31.678
Then all of a sudden, politics starts 
to enter into the thing.

00:12:31.678 --> 00:12:36.105
We already we've just come off of being lied
to for three years straight

00:12:36.105 --> 00:12:40.300
that Trump was a Russian agent, 
a traitor to the country.

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:46.880
So I think that that was that people looked
askance at that whole messaging system.

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:55.204
The underlying problem is that there are two
diametrically opposed views

00:12:55.204 --> 00:12:59.089
of what America should be like in this world

00:12:59.089 --> 00:13:02.700
and one is held by one side and 
one is held by the other

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:06.520
so you decide which one 
you’re going to be on.

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:11.860
You get into this situation where elite politicians
in the respective parties feel like they have

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:13.550
to polarize on the issue

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:17.111
because their base expects them to disagree
with the other party.

00:13:17.111 --> 00:13:22.740
It would have helped a great deal of the elites
of the political leaders of our country had

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:24.110
coordinated across party lines

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:26.194
and laid out a unified message at the beginning

00:13:26.194 --> 00:13:30.680
I definitely think we could have largely mitigated
the polarized responses 

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:32.250
that we saw in the mass public.

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:35.839
What do you hope for, what do you fear, 
when it comes to

00:13:35.839 --> 00:13:38.575
polarization around public health issues?

00:13:38.575 --> 00:13:41.700
One of the things I really worry about 
going forward is

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:46.060
what we’d like is reduced polarization around
Covid vaccination

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:50.672
especially as we move into a possible regular
regime of boosting going forward.

00:13:50.672 --> 00:13:55.779
But what I think might be more likely if we
aren't really, really effective and proactive

00:13:55.779 --> 00:13:57.430
on reducing that polarization

00:13:57.430 --> 00:14:01.890
is that polarization around Covid vaccination
persists and spreads to other vaccines like

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:03.945
measles, mumps, rubella.

00:14:03.945 --> 00:14:08.398
And sure enough, researchers at UC San Diego
tracked vaccine attitudes 

00:14:08.398 --> 00:14:10.616
from March to August 2021

00:14:10.616 --> 00:14:14.080
and they found that not only were the Republicans
in their study more likely to turn against

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:16.269
the Covid vaccine as the year went on

00:14:16.269 --> 00:14:20.418
they also ended up with declining attitudes
about vaccines in general 

00:14:20.418 --> 00:14:24.000
and lower intentions to get 
the flu shot next year.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:31.770
Which means the health consequences of pandemic
polarization could extend well beyond Covid-19.

